t the MID Server successfully in certain conditions (mostly when there are too many running or hung threads","line":176},{"title":"PRB1396562 / KB0861153 MID Server Upgrade log shows error for \"The ServiceNow Platform Distribution Upgrade (xxx) service is not installed - The specified service does not exist as an installed service\", that does not break anything","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0861153 \"PRB1396562 / KB0861153 MID Server Upgrade log shows error for \\\"The ServiceNow Platform Distribution Upgrade (xxx","line":177},{"title":"PRB1422003 / KB0861154 MID Upgrade does not support changing the temp directory of the JVM (antivirus/security blocking temp folder during upgrade)","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0861154 \"PRB1422003 / KB0861154 MID Upgrade does not support changing the temp directory of the JVM (antivirus/security blocking temp folder during upgrade","line":178},{"title":"KB1002245 / PRB1449497 Null pointer exception when MID Server shuts down after Validating","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB1002245 \"KB1002245 / PRB1449497 Null pointer exception when MID Server shuts down after Validating\"","line":179},{"title":"KB0999273 / PRB1538125 Mid Server fails to check that the temporary Upgrade process is running properly before shutting itself down, causing MID Server Down","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB0999273 \"KB0999273 / PRB1538125 Mid Server fails to check that the temporary Upgrade process is running properly before shutting itself down, causing MID Server Down\"","line":180},{"title":"KB0749292 / PRB1314105 During the MID upgrade 2 minutes time-out for deleting old files is not enough for some customers","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0749292 \"KB0749292: PRB1314105 During the MID upgrade 2 minutes time-out for deleting old files is not enough for some customers\"","line":181},{"title":"KB0715612 / PRB1307275 MID Server auto-upgrade will fail if Windows has 'Application Experience' disabled","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0715612 \"KB0715612 / PRB1307275 MID Server auto-upgrade will fail if Windows has 'Application Experience' disabled\"","line":182},{"title":"KB0743123 / PRB1330396 MID Server start.bat fails to check if a Windows Service already exists for the installation folder before creating another service","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0743123 \"KB0743123 /PRB1330396 MID Server start.bat fails to check if a Windows Service already exists for the installation folder before creating another service\"","line":183},{"title":"KB0827747 / PRB1408516 MID Server upgrade fails leaving MID Server Down, due to Cisco AMP antivirus preventing the upgrade service deleting the Wrapper executable","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0827747 \"KB0827747 / PRB1408516 MID Server upgrade fails leaving MID Server Down, due to Cisco AMP antivirus preventing the upgrade service deleting the Wrapper executable\"","line":184},{"title":"KB0715244 / PRB1279578 MID server auto-upgrade fails while copying files from temp to agent folder on Windows even with ''Application Experience' enabled","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0715244 \"KB0715244: Known Error PRB1279578: MID server auto-upgrade fails while copying files from temp to agent folder on Windows even with ''Application Experience' enabled\"","line":185},{"title":"KB0719830 Is OpenJDK supported as the JRE for MID Servers, and which versions/patches can I use?","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0719830 \"KB0719830 Is OpenJDK supported as the JRE for MID Servers, and which versions/patches can I use?\"","line":186},{"title":"KB0750004 / PRB1320637 A MID Server upgrade that includes a new JRE version will overwrite the cacerts file","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0750004 \"KB0750004 / PRB1320637 A MID Server upgrade that includes a new JRE version will overwrite the cacerts file\"","line":187},{"title":"KB0779816 How to continue a MID Server upgrade after it has crashed in the middle of the ServiceNow Platform Distribution Upgrade service, leaving the MID Server Down and the Service not running","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0779816 \"KB0779816 How to continue a MID Server upgrade after it has crashed in the middle of the ServiceNow Platform Distribution Upgrade service, leaving the MID Server Down and the Service not running\"","line":188},{"title":"KB0858627 / PRB1419577 The MID Server Upgrade service doesn't properly detect if the MID Server has fully shut down, and so has issues with file locks when it starts deleting, potentially leaving the MID Server down","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0858627 \"KB0858627 / PRB1419577 The MID Server Upgrade service doesn't properly detect if the MID Server has fully shut down, and so has issues with file locks when it starts deleting, potentially leaving the MID Server down\"","line":189},{"title":"KB0858554 / PRB1429834 MID Server down after attempted upgrade, due to file locks caused by Dell SecureWorks Red Cloak anti-virus (mid.bat, java.exe, wrapper-windows-x86-64.exe)","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0858554 \"KB0858554 / PRB1429834 MID Server down after attempted upgrade, due to file locks caused by Dell SecureWorks Red Cloak anti-virus (mid.bat, java.exe, wrapper-windows-x86-64.exe","line":190},{"title":"PRB1437357 / KB0861733 Upgrade fails leaving MID Server DOWN, due to antivirus/security software flagging InjectorService.exe as Malware/Trojan","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0861733 \"PRB1437357 / KB0861733 Upgrade fails leaving MID Server DOWN, due to antivirus/security software flagging InjectorService.exe as Malware/Trojan\"","line":192},{"title":"PRB1373214 / KB0784943 MID Server Down after auto-Upgrade service 10 minute file lock timeout: SEVERE: java.io.IOException: Unable to delete agent\\\\lib\\\\accessors-smart.jar","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0784943 \"PRB1373214 / KB0784943 MID Server Down after auto-Upgrade service 10 minute file lock timeout: SEVERE: java.io.IOException: Unable to delete agent\\lib\\accessors-smart.jar\"","line":193},{"title":"PRB1451866 / KB0869024 The fix for PRB1320637 requires that the cacerts Truststore file password remains as the default \"changeit\", which many customers won't allow, causing certificate deletion during JRE upgrades (e.g. Quebec) and subsequent MID Server and Integration outage","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB0869024 \"PRB1451866 / KB0869024 The fix for PRB1320637 requires that the cacerts Truststore file password remains as the default \\\"changeit\\\", which many customers won't allow, causing certificate deletion during JRE upgrades (e.g. Quebec","line":194},{"title":"KB0962099 / PRB1498314 MID server upgrade on Japanese Windows server fails leaving it DOWN with: Wrapper.stop() failed to stop the MID Server. Trying to use taskkill command to kill the process","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB0962099 \"7.14 KB0962099 / PRB1498314 MID server upgrade on Japanese Windows server fails leaving it DOWN with: Wrapper.stop(","line":195},{"title":"PRB1396562 / KB0861153 Latest Version MID Server Auto-Upgrade fails for JRE 11.0.11+ resulting in server shutdown","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB0719830 \"7.15 PRB1396562 / KB0861153 Latest Version MID Server Auto-Upgrade fails for JRE 11.0.11+ resulting in server shutdown\"","line":196},{"title":"KB1001745 / PRB1547917 Before shutting down for an upgrade, MID Server fails to confirm that it will be able to start itself again, or report the issue, leaving the MID Server Down","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB1001745 \"KB1001745 / PRB1547917 Before shutting down for an upgrade, MID Server fails to confirm that it will be able to start itself again, or report the issue, leaving the MID Server Down\"","line":197},{"title":"KB2788640 / PRB1979997 Windows MID Server fails to upgrade when installed on a non-English Windows server","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB2788640","line":198},{"title":"KB2398708 / PRB1898139 MID server not starting due to parentheses in the home folder's path, leaving MID Server Down after Upgrades","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&amp;sysparm_article=KB2398708","line":199},{"title":"KB2536752 PRB1942577 Mid Server with a closing parenthesis ')' in the windows service name, doesn't start itself after upgrading, leaving the MID Server Down","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB2536752","line":200},{"title":"KB0792621 / PRB1381000 MID Server service starts regardless of whether a failed Upgrade Service still remains, leading to deletion of the upgrade service, and potentially leaving the MID Server running in a semi-upgraded and corrupt state","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0792621 \"KB0792621 / PRB1381000 MID Server service starts regardless of whether a failed Upgrade Service still remains, leading to deletion of the upgrade service, and potentially leaving the MID Server running in a semi-upgraded and corrupt state\"","line":201},{"title":"KB0813636 / PRB1385357 MID Server can fail to install or upgrade to Orlando due to new external connectivity requirement to ocsp.entrust.net for OCSP certification revocation verification check","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0813636 \"KB0813636 / PRB1385357 MID Server can fail to install or upgrade to Orlando due to new external connectivity requirement to ocsp.entrust.net for OCSP certification revocation verification check\"","line":202},{"title":"KB0821436 / PRB1394171 Linux MID server auto-upgrade can fail even on Tanuki wrapper version 3.5.36 if MID service is not reinstalled","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0821436 \"KB0821436 / PRB1394171 Linux MID server auto-upgrade can fail even on Tanuki wrapper version 3.5.36 if MID service is not reinstalled\"","line":203},{"title":"KB0746874 / PRB1312206 Linux MID server upgrade fails, and MID Server remains Down, on upgrade to Madrid - Tanuki wrapper service shutdown as 'TERM Trapped'","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0746874 \"KB0746874 / PRB1312206 Linux MID server upgrade fails, and MID Server remains Down, on upgrade to Madrid - Tanuki wrapper service shutdown as 'TERM Trapped'\"","line":204},{"title":"KB0727033 MID Server won't start due to Root Certificate requirements - wrapper error \"The digital signature of the object did not verify\"","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0727033 \"KB0727033 MID Server won't start due to Root Certificate requirements - wrapper error \\\"The digital signature of the object did not verify\\\"\"","line":205},{"title":"KB0826461 / PRB1406629 After Upgrade to Orlando, MID Server fails to connect to Instance with \"last block incomplete in decryption\" if the proxy password is blank","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0826461 \"KB0826461 / PRB1406629 After Upgrade to Orlando, MID Server fails to connect to Instance with \\\"last block incomplete in decryption\\\" if the proxy password is blank\"","line":206},{"title":"PRB1396279 / KB0858646 File permissions enforcement removes permissions of the windows service's log on as user, when computer or domain name has lowercase letters, leaving MID Server down","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0858646 \"PRB1396279 / KB0858646 File permissions enforcement removes permissions of the windows service's log on as user, when computer or domain name has lowercase letters, leaving MID Server down\"","line":207},{"title":"PRB1435863 /  KB0861098 Mid Server DOWN due to false \"expected service name\" error, (1) if because of powershell issue the service name cannot be fetched or (2) if the 'case' of the Service Name not exactly matching between wrapper-override.conf and the running service/registry","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0861098 \"PRB1435863 /  KB0861098 Mid Server DOWN due to false \\\"expected service name\\\" error, (1","line":208},{"title":"PRB1437392 / KB0861829 Mid Server DOWN due to false \"expected service name\" error, if the checking script has a PSReadLine/PSConsoleReadLine error","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0861829 \"PRB1437392 / KB0861829 Mid Server DOWN due to false \\\"expected service name\\\" error, if the checking script has a PSReadLine/PSConsoleReadLine error\"","line":209},{"title":"PRB1447511 / KB0864241MID Server shows certificate chain errors with self-signed cert","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb_view.do?sysparm_article=KB0864241 \"PRB1447511 / KB0864241MID Server shows certificate chain errors with self-signed cert\"","line":210},{"title":"PRB1489024 / KB0959468 In Quebec : MID Server upgrade stops if Powershell tests in Pre-upgradecheck failed and Powerconsole remains busy and the closing the session failed","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB0959468 \"PRB1489024 / KB0959468 In Quebec : MID Server upgrade stops if Powershell tests in Pre-upgradecheck failed and Powerconsole remains busy and the c